"C:\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7\\pwsh.exe" -Command "@'
# T-008 — checkbox alignment (F12) and indent guides (F13)

Completed 2026-10-18. PASS. Writes confined to src/AntiQuickPad/, this report, T-008-*.png, and .coord/status-T008.md. No git, network, shared STATUS.md edits, or process termination.

## Implementation

CheckboxRenderer draws on KnownLayer.Selection over transparent three-character task markers. Removing the inline Border/Path means checkbox controls cannot enlarge text rows. The box centre uses the text-line baseline minus half the actual x-glyph height, matching StrikeRenderer's baseline calculation and fallback. The check path is centred by its ink extents, including round caps. Hit testing uses the drawn box rectangle; pointer hover sets the hand cursor and tooltip; left press toggles the underlying marker through the existing undoable document operation. Read-only editors still reject changes. Existing marker text advance remains intact.

IndentGuideRenderer implements IBackgroundRenderer on KnownLayer.Background, after the code panel and below text. It draws at every completed four-space indent level; tabs advance to four-space stops (editor indentation size explicitly set to 4). Guide positions use the relevant editor/code font's measured space advance. Look.ShowIndentGuides, Look.IndentGuide (#445160), and Look.IndentGuideThickness (1 DIP) control appearance. Column zero has no guide. Blank runs carry only the levels shared by the nonblank lines on both sides; trailing blanks and code/list block transitions stop the guides.

## Pixel proof

Both artifacts are real editor RenderTargetBitmap captures at 96 DPI / scale 1, 798 x 510 pixels. Both final PNGs were opened and visually inspected: check marks sit within their boxes, boxes align with bullets, row spacing stays even, and guides track the nested list/code indent columns. The white fence folding control and its separate margin connector are existing folding UI, not an indent guide.

- [T-008-checkbox.png](T-008-checkbox.png): "'`- [ ] open`, `- [x] done`, `- plain`, nested open/checked/plain rows.
- [T-008-guides.png](T-008-guides.png): nested lists, continuing and terminating blank lines, indented Python fence, and one/two leading tabs.

Measured from raster ink bounds (pixel edges):

| Checkbox row | Check centre delta X/Y vs box | Box centre delta Y vs bullet |
|---|---|---|
| 1 open | n/a | 1.00 px |
| 2 checked | 0.50 / 0.00 px | 1.00 px |
| 4 nested open | n/a | 0.50 px |
| 5 nested checked | 0.00 / 0.50 px | 0.50 px |

All checkbox and plain rows measure **22.917 DIP**. An additional all-plain raster control at identical indentation has **0.00 px maximum bullet-centre displacement** from checkbox rows, proving row placement is unchanged in pixels. Hit rectangles, hand cursor on/off, marker toggle, and undo pass the focused smoke checks. Physical pointer dispatch was not manually exercised.

Guide proof compares renderer-on/off rasters and independently measures expected four-space stops using FormattedText. Exactly one changed pixel column per guide: **column 4 -> x=82; column 8 -> x=122; column 12 -> x=162**. Nested list rows and their continuing blank have x=82/122; Python'"'s deepest body has x=82/122/162. The code-body blank continues x=82/122. End-of-list blanks, code-to-list transition blank, final blank and unindented rows have zero guide pixels. Tab rows have x=82 and x=82/122. An actual renderer with ShowIndentGuides=false produces a raster identical to the renderer-removed control.

